# Cursor access-block noise only — OK to block AI access entirely.
# LTM cold corpus lives in .rgignore + .cursorindexingignore (NOT here),
# so CATALOG → explicit archive/LTM Read paths stay reachable.

# .worktrees/ is dispatch_cursor.ps1's own designated worktree spot
# (Worktree = <repo>/.worktrees/<Slug>, per that script's own doc) -- a blanket
# block here made every cursor-fleet dispatch structurally unable to read its
# own pointer file (found 2026-08-20, dispatch b53dd04/aegis-3leg-risk-param:
# Cursor halted NEEDS_CONTEXT, traced the block to this exact rule, refused to
# fabricate a plan from the filename). Re-included below: block bare files
# dropped directly in .worktrees/, but allow descent into <slug>/ subdirs, so
# a dispatched agent can read what it was actually pointed at.
.worktrees/*
!.worktrees/*/
.claude/worktrees/
.venv/
.venv-research/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
